Description: Provides a comprehensive, state-aware toolkit for single-cell
    and spatial transcriptomics analysis built around the Bioconductor
    SingleCellExperiment class. It introduces a lightweight analysis-state
    contract to manage dependencies, active context, and provenance across
    workflows. Features include end-to-end preprocessing, dimensionality
    reduction, clustering, multi-backend integration, reference mapping,
    trajectory inference, differential expression and enrichment,
    differential abundance, cell-cell communication, metacell aggregation,
    spatial deconvolution, in-silico perturbation, and enhanced
    visualization. Interoperability with AnnData and legacy compatibility
    aliases are supported, but the primary design is centered on
    SingleCellExperiment-native analysis.
